<main class="page">
  <div class="content">
    <a href="/blog" class="back">← Back to Blog</a>
    
    <h1>Pulse v0.9.0 Released: The Clean Up</h1>
    <span class="date">January 24, 2025</span>
    
    <div class="body">
      <p class="lead">Pulse v0.9.0 focuses on code quality, maintainability, and runtime efficiency. We have gutted the massive inline script injection system in favor of a modern, modular runtime architecture.</p>
      
      <h3>🧹 Runtime Logic Extraction</h3>
      <p>In previous versions, the compiler injected ~150 lines of raw string helpers into <em>every single component</em> to handle primitives like `List` and `Show`. In v0.9, we moved this logic to a shared <code>/runtime/dom.js</code> library.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Bundle Size:</strong> Significantly reduced for apps with multiple components.</li>
        <li><strong>Readability:</strong> Generated code is now much cleaner and easier to debug.</li>
        <li><strong>Maintainability:</strong> Core DOM logic lives in a proper TypeScript file, not inside template strings.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>✨ Performance Comparison</h3>
      <p>The architecture shift continues our trend of prioritizing runtime efficiency.</p>
      
      <div class="table-container">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Metric</th>
              <th>v0.8 (Strict)</th>
              <th>v0.9 (Modular)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Compiler Strategy</strong></td>
              <td>String Injection</td>
              <td>Runtime Import</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Code Duplication</strong></td>
              <td>High (per component)</td>
              <td>None (Shared)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Debuggability</strong></td>
              <td>Low (eval hell)</td>
              <td>High (Sourcemaps)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

